<!--
  An actual plan at DOP 4: a hash join that spilled, fed by a scan whose rows were badly
  under-estimated, with per thread counters chosen so the aggregates, the skew and the estimate
  ratio all have known answers.

  The sort's four worker threads carry 100, 100, 100 and 700 rows: a thousand rows over four threads
  is an even share of 250, so the busiest thread's 700 is a skew of 2.8.
-->
